From 87413bfff2c2b8a576f7bf3e3b050f01072bd940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:17:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: two panel window policy, one DisplayArea group per
 screen (opt-in)

Gives the Surface Duo stock-shaped window handling: each screen is its own DisplayAreaGroup with a
TaskDisplayArea, so an app on a screen gets a plain screen sized configuration (1344x1892 on the Duo 2) and never
sees the hinge; home and spanned apps stay in the default task area that covers the display.

- DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider (config_deviceSpecificDisplayAreaPolicyProvider): builds the two groups when
  persist.sys.phh.duo.panels or persist.debug.phh.duo.panels is 1 on a Duo (Build.DEVICE duo/duo2); otherwise the
  platform default policy, so other devices and the default setting are unchanged. Read once at display creation.
- PanelGroup follows its physical screen from DuoPanelGeometry and crops its surface to the screen, so the
  ActivityRecordInputSink of an app (touchable region = its crop) no longer swallows touches meant for the other
  screen or for home.
- Z-order: after every visibility pass the home / spanned area goes above the screens only while a non-home root
  task in it is visible (recents, a spanned app), otherwise below.
- Home per screen: a Home action force-hides the focused screen's tasks (collected into the transition, followed by
  a visibility pass), so home shows through there and the other screen keeps its app. A touch moving focus to the
  home window is not a Home action (ATMS.setFocusedTask marks it).
- Launch routing: a launcher icon opens its app on the screen that contains the icon (intent source bounds), for
  new and for existing tasks, for any launcher. A minimized task launched again comes back.

Needs DuoPanelGeometry (previous patch). Tested on a Duo 2 on android-16.0.0_r4 with Launcher3 and Microsoft
Launcher as home. The default provider string is set in core/res config.xml for now; it only has an effect when the
property is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
